  "id": "thecodfather",
  "note": "THE CODFATHER: the fishmonger on Filament Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: no glazing at all. The building is a counter with a roof on it: a marble slab the\nfull width of the frontage, open to the street behind a canvas awning on two poles, with a\ncrushed-ice bed on the slab. The name is painted blue on white on the fascia.\n\nOne full storey of white glazed tile, pulled up to the yard line so the slab and the awning poles\nstand on it, with a fascia stood up past a low zinc vault so the name reads from the street. The\ncold store behind is taller, in grey panel, with the louvres, the condenser and a vent stack, and\nthe back of the tile is left open to the shore. Filament Yard's prose stacks returned crates\nagainst the front, so they are there.\n\nThe tile is authored at one storey (`flags.floors: 1`), so `h` is a single storey and the walls\nspend all of it. Built at half that, it read as a slab on the ground with the kit's roof hoarding\nstanding over it.",
  "pal": "ty_cod",
